---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
import Shot from './Shot.astro';
---

<section id="features" tabindex="-1" class="px-4 sm:px-6 py-20" aria-labelledby="features-heading">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <SectionHeading id="features-heading" lead="Review every change before it lands." detail="Then commit only what belongs together." />

    <div class="tile-grid tile-grid-split mt-12">
      <article class="tile">
        <div class="tile-stage has-shot">
          <Shot name="changes" alt="The Changes view with src/filter-tasks.js staged, the test and README changes not staged, and a commit message ready." />
        </div>
        <div class="tile-copy">
          <h3>Stage what belongs.</h3>
          <p>Stage files, folders, or everything at once. Leave unrelated edits for a later commit.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="tile">
        <div class="tile-stage has-shot">
          <Shot name="diff" alt="A syntax-highlighted diff of src/filter-tasks.js with removed lines in red and added lines in green, and its line counts and status letter in the header." />
        </div>
        <div class="tile-copy">
          <h3>Read every diff.</h3>
          <p>Syntax-highlighted split or unified diffs, with word-level changes and line wrapping when you need it.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="tile">
        <div class="tile-stage has-shot">
          <Shot name="history" alt="History narrowed to README.md, listing the three commits that changed it with the lines each added and removed." />
        </div>
        <div class="tile-copy">
          <h3>History, branches, and worktrees.</h3>
          <p>Explore commit history, or only the commits that changed one file, across renames. Switch branches, and give parallel work its own worktree instead of stashing.</p>
          <a href="/docs/features/" class="mt-3 inline-block text-sm text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">Git workflows guide</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="tile">
        <div class="tile-stage has-shot">
          <Shot name="preview" alt="The README of the sample repository rendered in Preview, with a feature list and a Mermaid flowchart of how a task moves." />
        </div>
        <div class="tile-copy">
          <h3>Preview more than code.</h3>
          <p>Open HTML, images, SVG, and Markdown with Mermaid diagrams in Preview to see them rendered, next to their code.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="tile">
        <div class="tile-copy flex h-full flex-col justify-end">
          <h3>Back to where you were.</h3>
          <p>Back and Forward return to each place as you left it, with the same tab, unfolded files, and scroll position. Hold or right-click an arrow to jump several steps. In a browser, every place has an address you can reload or bookmark.</p>
          <a href="/docs/interface/#back-and-forward" class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">Back and Forward</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="tile">
        <div class="tile-stage has-shot">
          <Shot name="palette" alt="The command palette on its Commands tab, with tabs for files, branches, commits, pull requests, runs, and repositories, and the g then letter key next to each section." />
        </div>
        <div class="tile-copy">
          <h3>Find anything from the keyboard.</h3>
          <p>Ctrl+K opens the command palette, and Ctrl+P its files. Its tabs find branches, commits, pull requests, workflow runs, and repositories. In every list, the arrow keys or J and K move and Enter opens; g and a letter opens a section.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
